--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Design derivations (no code copied)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adze's sandbox permission model — the two-axis split of sandbox mode
(read-only / workspace-write / full-access) from approval policy
(untrusted / on-request / never), plus writable-root configuration — is modeled
on the design used by OpenAI's Codex CLI (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/openai/codex). No code was copied.

Adze's edit-format taxonomy and per-model format selection are modeled on
Aider (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider). No code was copied.

Adze's "immutable system-context baseline per cache epoch" approach to prompt
assembly is modeled on the context architecture documented by opencode
(MIT, https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode). No code was copied.

Adze's benchmark isolation design — agent container with future git history
removed, and grading performed only on the committed diff inside a separate
verifier container — is modeled on DeepSWE v1.1 by Datacurve
(https://deepswe.datacurve.ai). No code was copied.

Adze's IDE build pipeline — a patch series applied to a pristine upstream
Code-OSS checkout, rather than a merged long-lived fork — is modeled on
VSCodium (MIT, https://github.com/VSCodium/vscodium).

